# Cache headers for the production static build (Task 8.2). Netlify-style
# _headers syntax — Vite copies public/ into dist/ verbatim, so this ships
# as dist/_headers. Most static hosts (Netlify, and Cloudflare Pages/others
# via a compatible syntax) read this file directly; for a host that doesn't,
# translate these same rules into its own config (e.g. Nginx `Cache-Control`
# response headers, an Apache `.htaccess`, or a Vercel `vercel.json`).
#
# /assets/* (JS, CSS, fonts) are content-hashed by Vite — a changed file
# always gets a new filename — so they are safe to cache aggressively and
# immutably for a year. HTML, the sitemap and robots.txt keep the default
# short/no-cache below so a new deploy is picked up immediately.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
